Jean starts with 30 lollipops. She eats 2 lollipops, so the remaining number of lollipops is $30 - 2 = 28$. Jean wants to package 2 lollipops in one bag. To find out how many bags she can fill, we divide the number of remaining lollipops by the number of lollipops per bag: $\frac{28}{2} = 14$. Therefore, Jean can fill 14 bags.

\boxed{14}

